{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And you shall sanctify him</b> — Two times in the Masorah: one at the beginning of a verse and one at the end of a verse: וקדשתו כי את לחם אלהים הוא מקריב. And the law: regarding a priest, at the beginning of a verse — because his sanctity is first: to open first, and to bless first, and to take a fine portion first. And a Torah scholar, his sanctity is at the end, as written: לקדושים אשר בארץ המה — meaning, after his death, when he is in the land, his sanctity is cut off, for in their lifetime they are among His holy ones — ובחייהם הן בקדושיו לא יאמין — and also the greatness of a Torah scholar is at the end of the reading, for the greatest of all rolls (the scroll)."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {0 "The second Masorah citation is Leviticus 21:8; the phrase לקדושים אשר בארץ המה is from Psalms 16:3. The phrase ובחייהם הן בקדושיו לא יאמין is textually difficult; rendered hyper-literally. The final word גולל (from גלל, to roll) likely refers to rolling the Torah scroll, i.e., the greatest scholar performs the hagbahah (lifting/rolling) at the end of the reading."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:13:43.171287867Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}